True, the width is 80 characters in most tty ports.
The score is shown on the first status line, so it doesn't really matter
for the additional stats that are shown on the second line.

I have showscore on in my config file and there is often some space
between your rank title and strength, because the game tries to reserve
enough space for the longest title of your class. When the line length
this way exceeds the space reserved (mostly 80 chars), that space between
the title and strength is the first thing that gets truncated. And if the
line would still be too long, the rank title is not displayed. 

I remember only having seen the rank title truncated with monks, and even
with them I have never seen anything further get truncated. Besides, the
score is the last thing on the line, so it would be the next thing to be
truncated anyway. I often turn the showscore off when I notice the
monk title getting truncated away.

